===Etymology===
From {{der|en|he|יִשְׁמָעֵאל||God hears, God will hear|tr=yishma'él (yišmāʿēl)}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɪʃ.meɪ.əl/|/ˈɪʃ.meɪl/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-JutishMale-Ishmael.wav|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q183403}}{{lb|en|Abrahamism|biblical character}} The eldest [[son]] of [[Abraham]] and his wife's handmaiden [[Hagar]] who were cast out after the [[birth]] of [[Isaac]]; [[traditionally]] the [[ancestor]] of the [[Arab]]s via the [[Ishmaelites]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Genesis|16|15|page=92|column=1|passage=And Hagar bare Abram a ſonne: and Abram called his ſonnes name, which Hagar bare, '''Iſhmael'''.}}
# {{given name|en|male|from=Hebrew}}.
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|chapter=Loomings|page=1|passage={{smc|Call}} me '''Ishmael'''.}}

